# CI and releases

After every push, PR update, merge, or tag: wait for GitHub Actions on that ref. Do not declare the work done while CI is queued, running, or red.

On failure: fix the root cause and harden (regression test, pin, timeout, fail-closed guard, diagnostic). Do not retry flakes away. Do not skip or override required checks.

PR chains: watch the last PR in the series, then the `main` push after that last merge. Do not leave `main` red.

Releases: `CHANGELOG.md` must contain every high-level change since the previous tag. Also write `docs/releases/vX.Y.Z.md` from `RELEASE-NOTES-TEMPLATE.md`. Tag only a green SHA. A red tag is a release blocker.

Record hardening in `docs/ci-failure-hardening/` using `CI-FAILURE-HARDENING-TEMPLATE.md`.
